    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.74) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.10) anchoring the lineup as our primary offensive engines. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a favorable matchup against the left-handed Weathers, bolstered by a strong xwOBA profile and an assumed high-leverage spot in the #2 hole. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a dynamic platoon advantage against Scott, making him a high-efficiency play. **Josh Jung** (68.56) is our standout dark horse; despite the uncertainty of a pending lineup, the combination of a soft matchup against Quintana (5.33 xERA) and a significant park factor boost makes him a critical start for Roto production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision centered on **Nolan Schanuel** (55.32), who remained on the outside looking in despite a solid profile against Ginn. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects as a reliable floor play, the optimizer favored the higher ceiling of **Brady House** (55.65) and the strategic stolen base potential elsewhere in the lineup. We are closely monitoring the status of **Gunnar Henderson** (49.79), whose score is suppressed by a tough matchup against Shane McClanahan. Although the 100% stolen base opportunity against McClanahan's slow delivery provides a slight buffer, he remains a candidate for mid-game substitution if the wind or early results don't tilt in our favor.\n\nWe remain wary of the risk inherent in today\u2019s \"Lineup Pending\" status, particularly for **Sam Antonacci** (45.42) and **Josh Lowe** (58.38), whose values are heavily dependent on confirmed batting order placement. While **Kyle Tucker** (65.33) provides elite stability in the middle of the order, owners should note that several of our peripheral bats, such as **Dominic Smith** (42.37), are hovering near our benching threshold. With **Luis Robert Jr.** still shelved on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the platoon advantages of our active starters to maintain efficiency, and we will be ready to pivot to **Coby Mayo** or **Miguel Vargas** should late-afternoon weather or lineup adjustments compromise our projected scoring floor.",
